              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Tampa's commercial trucks don't get a break from the road, and their parts don't either. Whether you need a new OEM component or a reliable used part to keep an older truck running, finding the right source matters as much as finding the right part.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For owner-operators and fleet managers in the Tampa area, that means knowing where to go before something breaks down, not scrambling to find it after. Here's what to look for and where Sun State International fits into that search.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-new-vs-used",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "New Parts vs. Used Parts: What's the Difference?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "new-vs-used"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-new-vs-used-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "New parts, whether OEM or aftermarket, come with predictable performance and a warranty behind them. They're the safer choice for critical systems like brakes, steering, and emissions components, where reliability isn't optional.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-new-vs-used-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Used parts can make sense for older trucks, discontinued models, or non-critical components where cost matters more than a warranty. The key is sourcing them from a dealer who inspects and verifies condition before selling, not a salvage yard with no accountability.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-what-to-look-for",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What to Look for in a Tampa Truck Parts Source",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "what-to-look-for"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-what-to-look-for-1",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "A large in-stock inventory of new and used parts for all makes and models"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Staff who can verify fitment before you buy"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Fast turnaround so your truck isn't sitting longer than it needs to"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "A service department that can install what they sell"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Straightforward pricing and honest guidance on new vs. used"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-to-look-for-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Tampa fleets that skip this step often end up with the wrong part, a part that doesn't hold up, or a part with no support behind it if something goes wrong.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
